{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory has no responsibility-chain error: the doctor immediately escalated the deep electrical burn with chills and odor to same-day emergency/burn evaluation, repeatedly screened systemic and wound danger signs, avoided unsafe self-medication or home debridement, reconciled discharge medications, and converted barriers into executable plans. Closure is safe as a valid open transition to outpatient burn follow-up with clear red flags, medication instructions, non-weight-bearing precautions, and caregiver involvement. Multiple high-order points were actively completed with trajectory impact, including misconception correction, hidden-risk/record-oriented discovery and integration, false-positive/false-negative verification around drainage/odor/temperature, and real-world barrier navigation. This satisfies the Perfect boundary.",
